[list]
[*]Apparel that has alternate looks can now be restyled where it sits. Ideology's styles, and the random variants on pieces like Anomaly's ritual masks, appear as a small button on the item's row: click it to cycle the looks, right-click for the full list. The base game only picks one of these when an item is made, and until now there was no way to change it afterwards.
[*]Colour and style are independent, so a restyled helmet keeps whatever paint you gave it, and a garment you have already painted can still be restyled.
[*]The button appears only on rows whose item actually has styles, so most of a stand's contents look exactly as before. In vanilla that means helmets, dusters, jackets, parkas, war masks and the cultist masks; style mods add their own.
[*]Styles come from the DLC that defines them, so what you can pick depends on what you own. The mod itself still requires none of them.
[*]Everything works where the Paint tab already did: outfit stands, Armor Racks and vanilla-style storage.
[*]Reel's Expanded Storage is confirmed working.
[/list]
